WEBVTT

NOTE Captions for the Braid showcase film (2026-08, 57.5s timeline).

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.600
(The Braid mark weaves across a dark stage.)

2
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:07.200
Stop alt-tabbing. Claude, Grok and Gemini — one table.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.000
All-at-once is on — the room is ready.

4
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.600
Ask once, in plain words.

5
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:17.600
Claude, Grok and Gemini take the question at the same time.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:20.800
Complete answers — one lap, done.

7
00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:23.200
Now make them argue. Squads — two sides, real rebuttals.

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.200
Pick Squads and set two laps.

9
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:28.470
Lap one — three positions, argued in full.

10
00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.730
Lap two — every seat reads every word, and strikes back.

11
00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:33.030
Gemini red-teams the other side by name.

12
00:00:33.030 --> 00:00:35.430
Claude concedes two hits — on the record.

13
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.030
Then the room settles it.

14
00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.430
Read the room your way.

15
00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:42.230
Stack — one document, in order.

16
00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.030
Thread — the room as a timeline.

17
00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:45.830
Side — three lanes, side by side.

18
00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:49.000
Loops — one pass, N laps, infinite, or run to a goal.

19
00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:52.600
Every seat and every model, on your phone.

20
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.500
BRAID — amni-scient.com/braid — open beta, ten dollars a month.
